  "method": "Retain every resolution-separated actual maximum, without a maximum-relative power cutoff or a fixed peak count. Review local prominence and absolute strain amplitude, then require consistent peak frequency/amplitude under a Blackman-window comparison to flag Hann leakage, and actual atom rebinning with a half-x-bin origin shift and neighboring Gaussian smoothing widths. Same-grain far-field signed strain uses the same x window, binning, baseline, z channel and physical power units. Shared far-field peaks are descriptive evidence and never a veto: elastic fields may extend into the far field. These are fixed review heuristics, not significance tests.",
